tom
===

This crate family is a Rust port of the TypeScript `pi` SDK, not a verbatim
copy of it.

Upstream projects
-----------------

    pi — https://github.com/earendil-works/pi
    Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner
    Licensed under the MIT License.

    pi-rust — https://github.com/bigfish1913/pi-rust
    Copyright (c) 2026 BigFish
    Licensed under the MIT License.

The `tom-*` crates descend from `pi-rust`, the Rust port of the original
MIT-licensed TypeScript `pi` SDK. `tom` is that port renamed: the crate
family, binary and configuration paths were renamed from `rpi` to `tom`, so
`pi-rust` is this repository's direct parent project. The license text in
`LICENSE` therefore carries the upstream copyright notices, the `pi-rust`
notice and the notice for the Rust port, as required by the MIT License's
retention clause.

Third-party dependencies
------------------------

Runtime dependencies and their licenses are listed by `cargo metadata` and on
each crate's crates.io page. Vendored or copied source, where it exists, keeps
its original attribution in the file header.
